<title>USA: RenalTreatment added to S&amp;P Smallcap 600.</title>
<headline>RenalTreatment added to S&amp;P Smallcap 600.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK, N.Y. 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Renal Treatment Centers Inc would replace American Medical Response Inc on the S&amp;P SmallCap 600 Index after the close of trading on February 14, the Equity Services Group of Standard &amp; Poor's said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>American Medical was being acquired by Laidlaw Inc in a cash tender offer scheduled to close on that date, the company said.</p>
<p>Renal Treatment provides dialysis to patients suffering from chronic kidney failure, mostly through its network of outpatient treatment centers and in patients' homes.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
